            <ArticleTitle>Anastomotic pseudoaneurysm after aorto-coronary bypass grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a pseudoaneurysm at the site of the distal anastomosis of a saphenous vein coronary bypass graft is described. The aneurysm was resected. To our knowledge this is the first report of this complication after coronary bypass surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
